-- title:
--   Modulus-one change of variables for twisted unipotent orbital integrals
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be an extension of number fields that is Galois, let the idele group $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ carry a Borel measurable structure and a Haar measure $\nu$, and let $\mathbb{A}_L$ carry its Borel structure and the additive Haar measure $\mu =$ `adelicAddHaar`. Let $D$ be a datum consisting of a monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{act}$ from $\mathrm{Aut}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$, each continuous, compatible with the Galois action on principal adeles, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Aut}(L/K)$ be such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$. Write $\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}$ for the entrywise automorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ induced by $\mathrm{act}\,\sigma$, $\iota$ for the entrywise map $\mathrm{GL}_2(L) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ along $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$, $c(z) = \mathrm{diag}(z,z)$ for $z \in (\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$, and $n(u) = \begin{pmatrix}1&u\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ for $u \in \mathbb{A}_L$. Let $\xi : (\mathbb{A}_L)^\times \to \mathbb{C}$ be continuous, let $t' \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ have vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries with $N_{L/K}(t'_{00}/t'_{11}) \neq 1$, let $\varphi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L) \to \mathbb{C}$ be continuous with compact support, and let $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$. Then three assertions hold simultaneously: first, the iterated lower integral in $[0,\infty]$ of $\|\xi(z)\|\,\|\varphi\big((n(s)y)^{-1}\,\iota(t')\,\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(c(z)\,n(s)\,y)\big)\|$, over $z$ against $\nu$ and then over $s$ against $\mu$, equals the iterated lower integral over $w$ against $\nu$ of $\|\xi(w)\|$ times the lower integral over $t$ against $\mu$ of $\|\varphi\big(y^{-1}\,\iota(t')\,\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(n(t)\,c(w)\,y)\big)\|$; second, this latter iterated lower integral is finite; third, the corresponding iterated Bochner integrals of the complex integrands $\xi(z)\varphi\big((n(s)y)^{-1}\iota(t')\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(c(z)n(s)y)\big)$ and $\xi(w)\int \varphi\big(y^{-1}\iota(t')\sigma_{\mathbb{A}}(n(t)c(w)y)\big)\,d\mu(t)$ agree.
--
--   This is the change of variables of modulus one by which a unipotent twisted orbital integral attached to a hyperbolic (diagonal, norm-regular) class in $\mathrm{GL}(2)$, written in conjugation form $\int F(n(s)y)\,d\mu(s)$, is converted into translation form, together with the absolute convergence that justifies it; no character property or $\sigma$-invariance of the weight $\xi$ is required. It is used in [`AutomorphicForm.setIntegral_mul_indicator_highSet_constantTerm_finsum_eq_indicator_mul_tsum_integral_unipotentGL2_twistedOrbital`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setIntegral_mul_indicator_highSet_constantTerm_finsum_eq_indicator_mul_tsum_integral_unipotentGL2_twistedOrbital), where the constant term of such a class is unfolded over the centre and the upper-triangular orbit into a sum of unipotent orbital integrals.
